Subject: [PATCH 1/4] =?UTF-8?q?feat(phase-9):=20patient=20erasure:=20anony?=
 =?UTF-8?q?mize,=20never=20delete=20(scope=20=C2=A78)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The mechanism pre-designed in mvp-scope §8, now built (backend only; how an
erasure is triggered is still to decide).

- Migration 0008: patients.anonymized_at, and patients_clinic_phone_key made
  partial (WHERE anonymized_at IS NULL) so erased records can share one
  placeholder number and a returning person gets a fresh record.
- Both patient upserts (online and staff booking) target the partial index.
- anonymizePatient(ctx, patientId), one transaction: overwrite name and
  phone, clear consent, cancel upcoming bookings (frees the slots), rotate
  every access-token hash so the patient's links die, one audit event with
  ids and counts only. No row is deleted; the clinic's history stays whole.
- updatePatient refuses an erased record, so an erasure can't be undone by
  an edit.

10 new tests (224 total). Migration applied to a real Postgres 16 with data;
the browser suite still passes on it.

