From a3c2acf8b47fe3e40c0828b888890f7128ef3302 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:58:28 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(booking): retry a deadlock between racing bookings
 instead of failing (F4)

Two transactions racing for one slot can be settled by Postgres with a
deadlock (40P01) rather than the exclusion violation (23P01). The booking
was safely refused either way, but the patient got a server error instead
of "that time was just taken". Online booking, patient reschedule, staff
booking and staff reschedule now retry a deadlocked transaction (max 3);
the retry fails cleanly with 23P01 and the normal slot_taken path answers.

Found by the race test on a local Postgres 16 (about 1 run in 6 failed);
after the fix, 15 of 15 integration runs clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NjUsEhNL3KvY6tfsuwmur8
