From 01f8570d72e81fd88f13618c9947440056aa343d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:21:50 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] refactor(phase-9): erasure uses a unique placeholder
 number; 0008 is additive only

Safer rollout. Swapping patients_clinic_phone_key for a partial index meant
old and new code each needed a different index, so no deploy order kept
bookings working. Instead, each erased record gets its own unassigned +999
number (11 random digits): erased records never collide on the existing
index, a returning person still gets a fresh record, and migration 0008 is
now only ADD COLUMN anonymized_at. Order: migrate, then deploy; the live
code ignores the new column.

Neither migration has been applied to production yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NjUsEhNL3KvY6tfsuwmur8
